{
  "slug": "artist:the-whispers",
  "name": "The Whispers",
  "editorial_article": "Formed in 1963 in Watts, California, The Whispers evolved from a local vocal group into a foundational R&B act. They relocated to the San Francisco Bay Area in 1966 at the invitation of Sly Stone, honing their live act before finding label success. Their mid-1970s period saw them recording in Philadelphia, where songwriters like Allan Felder and Norman Harris contributed tracks such as 'A Mother for My Children'. The group later signed to Dick Griffey's SOLAR Records in 1978, securing their first R&B chart-topper with 'And the Beat Goes On' in 1979. They continued their success throughout the 1980s with the 1987 R&B hit 'Rock Steady'. With fifteen top-ten R&B singles, the group remains a central figure in R&B history, having been inducted into the National Rhythm and Blues Hall of Fame in 2014.",
